-- title:
--   Asymptotics for affine floor sampling
-- statement:
--   For real a > 0 and any real b, the natural floor ⌊a x + b⌋₊ tends to infinity as x tends to infinity, and its real cast divided by x tends to a. If f n / n^d tends to L, then f ⌊a x + b⌋₊ / x^d tends to L a^d.
-- source:
--   OpenAI math, commit adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Polynomials/SimplexFloor.lean#L9-L45

